SUMMARY:November Book du Mois!
LOCATION:Cavalier House Books\, 302A Jefferson St
DESCRIPTION:CHB Lafayette is reading The Sentence by Louise Erdrich for its
  November Book du Mois!\nWe’ll meet at 6:15 p.m. on Nov. 24 (a Tuesday!)
  at the bookstore to discuss Erdrich’s novel!\nPop by the bookshop to ge
 t your copy\, or order online!: The Sentence: A Novel\nSynopsis:\nLouise E
 rdrich's latest novel\, The Sentence\, asks what we owe to the living\, th
 e dead\, to the reader and to the book. A small independent bookstore in M
 inneapolis is haunted from November 2019 to November 2020 by the store's m
 ost annoying customer. Flora dies on All Souls' Day\, but she simply won't
  leave the store. Tookie\, who has landed a job selling books after years 
 of incarceration that she survived by reading "with murderous attention\,"
  must solve the mystery of this haunting while at the same time trying to 
 understand all that occurs in Minneapolis during a year of grief\, astonis
 hment\, isolation\, and furious reckoning.\nBook du Mois is CHB Lafayette'
 s monthly book club! A CHB Bookseller leads the discussion\, and we vote a
 t our meetings for our upcoming monthly picks.\n\nhttps://www.downtownlafa
 yette.org/event/november-book-du-mois
URL:https://www.downtownlafayette.org/event/november-book-du-mois
